The post-pandemic instinct was to add buffer stock everywhere. It protected service levels and quietly destroyed working capital.

## Place Buffers Where Variance Lives

Variance is concentrated. Positioning inventory at the few nodes with the widest lead-time spread delivers most of the protection at a fraction of the cost.

## Measure What Matters

Track time-to-recover and time-to-survive per node. Together they show where the network is fragile long before a disruption proves it.
